86: ## V2. The retained fibres and the selected zero
87: 
88: At every retained multiplicative fibre the actual source
89: translation is transitive on its components by K13/K19.
90: Equation (VL.4) makes the coefficients of \(D\) equal on
91: that orbit. Hence \(D\) is an integral multiple of the
92: whole fibre there. At a retained reduced additive fibre,
93: the same transitivity proof K15 gives the same conclusion:
94: the reduced components form one orbit, so the equal
95: coefficients again give the whole fibre. At a smooth or
96: irreducible fibre this conclusion is immediate.
97: 
98: Every nonreduced additive fibre has been placed inside
99: one of the required cap discs in the complete sphere
100: tuples. Thus, outside those cap discs, all of \(D\) is a
101: sum of whole fibres. Their defining base monomials make
102: (VL.5) a base line-frame change, with its exact integral
103: winding retained in the collar. At the selected \(I_1\)
104: zero the same statement applies, since its full reduced
105: fibre has one component. A local coefficient \(kF\)
106: gives the actual torus-frame map
107: \((Z,V,q)\mapsto(Z,q^kV,q)\). On the cone-height lattice
108: it is
109: \[
110:  \widetilde L_k(v,h)=(v+k h\,\delta,h).
111:  \tag{VL.6}
112: \]
113: On the height-one fan it translates every vertex by
114: \(k\delta\). The whole-\(I_1\), simple-zero period lattice
115: is the full index-one lattice by K20, so this is an
116: actual period reindexing. More explicitly, it carries
117: every cone by \(\widetilde L_k\), with chart pullback
118: \(\chi^a\mapsto\chi^{\widetilde L_k^*a}\). These maps
119: commute with all face localizations and with the
120: actual deck maps. They extend (VL.5) holomorphically
121: on the carried charts. The differences of fan vertices
122: and the line cocharacter \(\delta\) are unchanged.
123: Thus its coefficient pair in the actual edge basis
124: and the fan integer are retained.
125: 
126: This statement does not set \(D\) equal to zero. Its
127: canonical section gives (VL.5), and its full-fibre
128: coefficients remain in the base-line transition functions.
129: 
130: ## V3. The capped fibres and their actual root lines
131: 
132: Use K19's actual quotient to remove a zero-gamma normal
133: root kernel. This changes the source coordinate and the
134: line frame by the displayed quotient maps and leaves a
135: primitive effective cap. It does not leave a hidden
136: elliptic isogeny or finite line character. On its minimal
137: root source, K15 proves that its actual line \(N\) has
138: degree zero on every component of the reduced central
139: fibre. Its generic Picard point is the pullback \(aG'\).
140: The corresponding constructed root line \(N_0\) has
141: the same point and the same zero component degrees.
142: 
143: The proper direct-image evaluation for
144: \(N\otimes N_0^{-1}\), rigidified on a regular fibre,
145: gives a base line and an effective vertical evaluation
146: divisor \(E\). The intersection of \(E\) with every
147: component is zero. The actual connected Kodaira
148: intersection matrix has integral kernel the whole
149: fibre multiplicity vector. Its components here are
150: reduced and their multiplicities have greatest common
151: divisor one. Consequently the evaluation divisor is
152: an integral whole-fibre divisor. Division by its
153: actual base monomial yields the line isomorphism
154: \[
155:              N\simeq N_0\otimes f_{\rm root}^*L_{\rm root}.
156:  \tag{VL.7}
157: \]
158: This is the direct-image map of K15, applied to these
159: two actual root lines; it retains their resolutions
160: and their marked generic Picard point.
161: 
162: Transport the actual affine source action to the
163: constructed root source by F44 or F49, including the
164: transported blowup centres in the quadratic case.
165: Those maps retain the entire outer annulus. Apply
166: (VL.7) before comparing the line lifts. On each
167: proper punctured root fibre, the ratio of two line
168: isomorphisms over the same source map is a
169: holomorphic nonzero function on that fibre, hence
170: constant there. It is therefore a base unit.
171: The conjugated suspension map agrees with the
172: representative suspension on the punctured root by
173: V1, hence on the full root by holomorphic extension.
174: The remaining ratio for the finite-deck lift
175: therefore has norm one.
176: The exact scalar averaging in F44/F49 removes its
177: norm-one base-unit coboundary and retains its finite
178: deck character.
179: 
180: Changing a root frame by \(z^k\) changes the deck
181: character by \(\zeta_m^k\). Keep both of these
182: quantities. The canonical source map (VL.5), the
183: actual root evaluation (VL.7), and their base-unit
184: ratio therefore give precisely the integer delta
185: collar and finite-character data already retained
186: in F44/F49 and K32. In particular the source
187: vertical coefficients supported inside a removed
188: cap are processed through its actual root divisor
189: diagram; they are not discarded from the line.
190: 
191: ## V4. Page and return comparison
192: 
193: The preceding maps identify the actual ordinary
194: source pieces and every actual root-cap line with
195: the constructed data, together with the displayed
196: base line and retained finite characters. They
197: commute with the suspension lift after the constant
198: scalar reparametrization in V1. All maps are fixed
199: while that scalar varies. Their outer annular
200: maps are exactly the ones used to glue the family.
201: 
202: Pull them to the actual one- or two-cap page of
203: K26/K28/K32. The remaining line ratio is the base
204: pullback in K32's evaluated line comparison. On
205: the compact page its class is \(kF\), and
206: \[
207:  c_1(N_{\rm page})F=F^2=0,\qquad
208:  (c_1(N_{\rm page})+kF)^2=c_1(N_{\rm page})^2 .
209:  \tag{VL.8}
210: \]
211: On the regular binding, the remaining base-line
212: transition is the one from an extending ordinary
213: disc, and the fibre degree is zero. The exact
214: relative boundary-gauge formula of K5/K32 gives
215: zero square ambiguity, including odd gauges.
216: The corresponding source isomorphism carries
217: the stable tangent pairing.
218: 
219: At the selected toric zero the monomial map of V2
220: and its extending base unit carry the entire Cox
221: product and the three complex curve labels. K27/K30's
222: explicit normal-coordinate comparison applies to
223: this transported product. On its normal three-plane
224: the residual bounded character contributes the
225: extending constant rotation loop already calculated
226: there. Thus the same individual pair and relative
227: coordinates are obtained in the transported fan
228: and framing. The K31 common-exterior recurrence
229: then retains the same fan integer.
